        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style='box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;height:100%;padding:28px;background:#ffffff;font-family:system-ui;color:#0f172a'><h1 style='margin:0 0 12px;font:800 26px/1.2 system-ui'>Detail</h1><p style='margin:0 0 12px;max-width:60ch;font:400 16px/1.6 system-ui;color:#334155'>This is the background a graph is rendered on -- the passive surface this node presents when it's seen from outside itself: referenced in a workspace, shown collapsed, browsed past rather than opened.</p><p style='margin:0;max-width:60ch;font:400 16px/1.6 system-ui;color:#334155'>It owns this content directly, same as every node's Detail view -- one Surface off the Declaration, leading detail, then icon, ending in a Glyph. What this template actually teaches lives on its landing content, reached by opening the graph itself, not by delegating this background to it.</p></div>"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
